Design for Hazardous Material Isolation requires the designer to identify all hazardous substances within the product (batteries, mercury switches, lead solder, brominated flame retardants, refrigerants, etc.) and design the product architecture so these materials are physically segregated, clearly marked, and accessible for early removal during disassembly. The goal is to prevent contamination of recoverable components and materials during the remanufacturing process. Hazardous components should be positioned for priority extraction in the disassembly sequence.